{"name":"Green Dynasty","hex":"#00988e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"dynasty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of rulers or dynasts from one family.","A family considered over time, with its ancestors and descendants"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynasty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dynasty","blocks":[{"text":"A dynasty is a sequence of rulers from the same family, usually in the context of a monarchical system, but sometimes also appearing in republics. A \"house\" is an imperial, royal or noble family, not always ruling. \nHistorians periodize the histories of many states and civilizations, such as the Roman Empire, Imperial Iran, Ancient Egypt (3100–30 BCE), and Ancient and Imperial China, using a framework of successive dynasties. As such, the term \"dynasty\" may be used to delimit the era during which a family reigned."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/The_Imperial_Family_of_Japan%2C_2021.jpg/330px-The_Imperial_Family_of_Japan%2C_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynasty","wikidata":"Q164950"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Spanish royal family of the House of Bourbon dates its roots to the Capetian dynasty of the 9th century, thus making it the oldest still reigning dynasty in Europe (photograph of King Felipe VI, Queen Letizia, the Princess of Asturias and her younger sister Infanta Sofía, in 2019)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrder_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Maria_Theresia_im_Kreise_ihrer_Familie.jpg/